        ],
        "text": "If you know enough CSS to identify an element by its tag, id (`#`), or class (`.`), you can add the `:hover` selector to make the changes only appear when the user has moused over an element.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\nYou can also target a specific `<span>` using a class or ID:\n\n```css\n/* By class */\n.my-span:hover {\n  color: blue;\n}\n\n/* By ID */\n#my-span:hover {\n  color: green;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: Inline JavaScript with `onmouseover` / `onmouseout`\n\nYou can use inline event handlers directly on the HTML element:\n\n```html\n<span\n  onmouseover=\"this.style.color='red';\"\n  onmouseout=\"this.style.color='black';\"\n>\n  Hover over me!\n</span>\n```\n\n",
